llm_answer:
Both $\alpha$ and $ eta$ decrease when there is increasing heterogeneity in the effective microbial death rate. Conversely, both $\alpha$ and $ eta$ increase when the expectation of the effective microbial death rate increases. The influence of randomness in the effective microbe mortality $\lambda$ on infectivity can be shown by expressing the parameters $\hat{\alpha}$ and $\hat{ eta}$ in terms of the mean ($\mu_\lambda$) and variance ($
u_\lambda$) of the effective death rate as $\hat{\alpha} =  rac{\mu_\lambda}{
u_\lambda}$ and $\hat{ eta} =  rac{\mu_\lambda^2}{
u_\lambda}$.
